      "writtenOn": "2022-09-08T13:45:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, as I was reading this, I came to the same conclusion about prototyped module functions. Those are probably less common, but I could see us stumbling into this bug again if someone wants to organize the graphite modules down the road. Is the actual answer: Any function that has a definition? If so, could we just adjust how we do this completely - rather than putting the flag in modifiers like this, change the implementation of FunctionCall::hasProperty here: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/skia/src/sksl/ir/SkSLFunctionCall.cpp;l\u003d847;drc\u003da442c20f87b3f20ec085cc20f86938f82b8c6914\n\n???",
      "parentUuid": "039cc420_0f563be0",
      "revId": "e642e21d20391a291cb2da1519b85e7ba9bd3ab9",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
